I cannot show you the exact markup used by the specific "harness" tool you mentioned, as I do not have access to your project or its source code. The markup for tool blocks would depend on the specific framework or library you are using.

However, I can provide a general example of how you might structure a tool block in HTML with a basic CSS style. This is not specific to any tool or harness, but it should give you a starting point:

```html
<div class="tool-block">
  <h3 class="tool-block__title">Tool Title</h3>
  <p class="tool-block__description">Description of the tool.</p>
  <a href="https://example.com/tool-page" class="tool-block__link">Learn more</a>
</div>
```

And a simple CSS style:

```css
.tool-block {
  border: 1px solid #ccc;
  padding: 1rem;
  margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
}

.tool-block__title {
  font-size: 1.25rem;
  margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
}

.tool-block__description {
  font-size: 0.9rem;
  color: #666;
  margin-bottom: 1rem;
}

.tool-block__link {
  display: inline-block;
  padding: 0.5rem 1rem;
  background-color: #007bff;
  color: #fff;
  border-radius: 0.25rem;
  text-decoration: none;
}
```
